{
  "name": "seal",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-06, the sculpt overlay; generator scratchpad sc/sea3/gen/seal.py): a HARBOUR SEAL (Phoca vitulina), 1.7 m nose to tail and its hind flippers 0.25 m more -- a plump spindle with no waist at the neck, the belly a little flattened; a round dog-like head, a domed cranium over a marked stop and a SHORT broad muzzle, the puffy whisker pads making a W at the front, the dark nose with its V-shaped NOSTRILS, big dark eyes, EAR HOLES and no ear flaps, pale beaded whiskers. Short furred FORE FLIPPERS with five claws, held against the flank; the HIND FLIPPERS point back and cannot turn under it, two fans of five webbed digits held palm to palm, the outer digits longest. Its coat a per-pixel pattern (coatpat.js `seal`): grey to brown above, densely spotted dark, paler and sparsely spotted beneath. `coats`: three harbour seals (silver grey, dark, brown) and two GREY SEALS (`greyseal`: the long straight Roman muzzle with no stop, parallel nostrils, blotched instead of spotted -- a dark bull at 1.25x, a pale cow). In the world (haulout.js): groups hauled out on the shore, lying with the head up, now and then galumphing down into the water, swimming, bottling with the head out, and hauling out again. SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- fclaw, hclaw (10 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur. WHISKERS (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sharp/whiskers.py): 14 @whisker-coloured whiskers a side, 4 rows on the whisker pad (70-100 mm); 2 @whisker-coloured whiskers a side, a brow tuft (45-55 mm) -- `whiskers` shapes (bodyspec.js whiskerStrands: thin pointed strands, mirrored, on the head, near mesh only; details, so every coat and variant still shares one mesh), replacing the hand-placed cones.",
